# C32 remediation after attempt-19 (9/8/9/8/8, fail)

| Finding | Remediation | Where |
|---|---|---|
| R1 a provisional `returned: false` removed recovery records before the send's final outcome | The core now says where each named send stands: `TakenSubmission.state` (`SubmissionState`) is `pending` while it is taken but not handed to the engine (a sign-in renewal or the write confirmation under way), `delivered` once its message entered the transcript, and `returned` when it was given back (failed renewal, declined write confirmation, a stop overtaking a renewal) or failed without an engine. Delivery is recorded by the engine session as each message enters the transcript (`Progress.messages`, newest 64), so it holds after the transcript drops its oldest entries. The page settles nothing on `pending`: a Not confirmed record or a tracked send waits for `delivered` or `returned`; an admitted receipt still clears the box of exactly what was sent (unless already returned), and the tracker then keeps the text if it is given back. A tracked send whose conversation is no longer shown before its final word (retired by A/B/A, cleared, replaced) becomes a Not confirmed record with its exact text, across remounts; nothing is sent by itself. Tests: "a pending report is never final: a send later given back keeps its exact text beside newer edits, on both send paths and through an A/B/A that retires its conversation" (pending then returned without the unsent text, on the current-conversation and first-send paths, with a newer edit and a remount; and an A/B/A retirement while renewing; fails without the fix); `a_renewal_restarts_with_changes_only_once_the_operator_allows_them_again` now names its three sends and checks pending while the confirmation is asked, then returned (declined), delivered (allowed) and returned (a stop while asking); the lost-receipt, returned-before-receipt and submission-ID ordering regressions are retained | `session.rs`, `harness_domain.rs`, `client.ts`, generated `TakenSubmission`/`SubmissionState`, `harness.tsx`, provenance P50 |

Attempt-19's first check run kept core-fixture flake logs under full-suite load (engine start-up timeouts in harness_process, runtime_changes confirmation, workbench_documents imports), each target passing alone; the same-input rerun passed.

B1/E1 (the C29 live Vulture verification receipt) stay owner-gated (`evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md`).
